The upstream Docker-derived profile permits clone, setns and unshare so non-root Chromium can
create its sandbox without CAP_SYS_ADMIN. Ryph adds an explicit clone3 -> ENOSYS (errno 38)
rule so modern glibc falls back to the allowed clone call rather than failing with EPERM.
Ryph also permits chroot without the outer CAP_SYS_CHROOT condition: Chromium's
sandbox/linux/services/credentials.cc ChrootToSafeEmptyDir uses it inside a fresh user
namespace. The kernel still requires the capability inside that namespace; the outer
container drops ALL capabilities. Chromium's namespace sandbox uses USER/PID/NET namespaces,
not a mount namespace; mount remains capability-gated (and therefore denied here).
Formatting is normalized to the repository style. The policy remains deny-by-default.
